    {
      "title": "Average car loan size jumps 49% in 7 years as buyers shift to SUVs",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/finance/news/average-car-loan-size-jumps-49-to-8-2-lakh-as-buyers-shift-to-suvs-126101300995_1.html",
      "description": "TransUnion CIBIL data shows average passenger-vehicle loan sizes rose 49 per cent between H1 2019 and H1 2026, while repayment tenures increased by five months to 62 months",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-13T12:17:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "Average loan size for PVs rises 49% to ₹8.2 lakh in 7 years: Report",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/auto/average-loan-size-for-pvs-rises-49-to-8-2-lakh-in-7-years-report-126101300734_1.html",
      "description": "The average passenger vehicle loan amount rose 49 per cent to Rs 8.2 lakh in the first half of 2026 from the corresponding period in 2019, while the average repayment tenure rose by five months to 62 months, suggesting rising car prices and consumer aspirations, a TransUnion CIBIL report said on Tuesday.\nAccording to the report, 'Shifting Gears 2026- Credit Drives Today's Mobility', premiumisation, driven by demand for SUVs and feature-rich cars, was extending beyond metropolitan cities, with 51 per cent of borrowers taking loans for higher-value cars in the January-June period coming from semi-urban and rural areas.\nNBFCs continued to lead vehicle financing, accounting for 73 per cent of two-wheeler loans and 37 per cent of passenger vehicle loans.\nThe active passenger vehicle borrower base reached 2.5 crore as of June 2026, 1.7 times the June 2019 level. Delinquency in passenger vehicle loans, measured by balances overdue for more than 90 days, declined to 0.5 per cent from the ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-13T10:21:28"
    }
  ]
